@startuml trading-data
' Render with: plantuml -tpng docs/Design/SoftArchitecture/figures/trading-data.puml
!include style.iuml
set separator none
title Trading module: its records, errors and tables

package "service.py" {
  class TradeRequest <<data>> {
    + request_id: UUID
    + symbol: str
    + trade_type: "buy"
    + quantity: int, above 0
    + expected_price: Money
  }
  class PortfolioValue <<data>> {
    + cash_balance: Money
    + holdings: HoldingValue[]
    + holdings_value: Money
    + total_value: Money
  }
}

package "routes.py" {
  class TradeReceipt <<data>> {
    + trade_id: UUID
    + status: str
    + unit_price: Money
    + currency_amount: Money
    + executed_at: datetime
    + cash_balance: Money
    + {static} of(trade): TradeReceipt
  }
  class PortfolioReply <<data>> {
    + simulated: true
  }
}

package "types.py" {
  class HoldingValue <<public>> {
    + symbol: str
    + quantity: int
    + price: Money
    + quoted_at: datetime
    + obtained_at: datetime
    + delayed: bool
    + value: Money
  }
  class RequestIdReusedError <<error>> {
    + code = "request_id_reused"
  }
  class MarketClosedError <<error>> {
    + code = "market_closed"
  }
  class PriceOutOfDateError <<error>> {
    + code = "price_out_of_date"
  }
  class PriceChangedError <<error>> {
    + code = "price_changed"
    + price: Decimal
  }
}

package "models.py" {
  class "Trade (trades)" as Trade <<table>> {
    + trade_id: UUID
    + request_id: UUID
    + portfolio_id: UUID
    + asset_id: UUID
    + trade_type: str
    + quantity: int
    + unit_price: Decimal
    + currency_amount: Decimal
    + cash_balance_after: Decimal
    + status: str
    + balance_change_id: UUID
    + created_at: datetime
    .. the database refuses ..
    a second (portfolio_id, request_id)
    a balance_change_id used twice
    currency_amount ≠ quantity × unit_price
    quantity ≤ 0, unit_price ≤ 0
    cash_balance_after < 0
    trade_type other than 'buy'
    status other than 'executed'
  }
  class "Holding (holdings)" as Holding <<table>> {
    + portfolio_id: UUID
    + asset_id: UUID
    + quantity: int
    .. the database refuses ..
    a second row for one stock
    quantity < 0
  }
}

PortfolioReply -up-|> PortfolioValue
PortfolioValue o-- HoldingValue
TradeReceipt ..> Trade : built from

HoldingValue -[hidden]down- RequestIdReusedError
RequestIdReusedError -[hidden]right- MarketClosedError
PriceOutOfDateError -[hidden]right- PriceChangedError
RequestIdReusedError -[hidden]down- PriceOutOfDateError

note bottom of Holding
  Both tables are deleted with their portfolio.
  Foreign keys are strings, such as "assets.asset_id",
  so trading never imports another module's models.py.
end note

legend right
  <color:#0F6E56>■</color> Public: what other modules may import
  <color:#185FA5>■</color> Data: a read-only record, or a table
  <color:#A32D2D>■</color> Error: a DomainError with status 409
  + anyone holding one may use it
  A hollow arrowhead means "is a".
  A diamond means "holds".
endlegend
@enduml
